    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nJump2d\n\n### Description\n\nHey, I'm trying to create custom mappings for `MiniJump2d.built_opts.single_character` but as soon as I change some options, it starts to behave weirdly: either it doesn't find spots, or it finds the wrong ones.\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.9.1\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. `nvim -u NONE` \r\n2. `:lua require('mini.jump').setup()`\r\n3. `:lua MiniJump2d.start(vim.tbl_deep_extend(\"force\", MiniJump2d.builtin_opts.single_char, {allowed_lines = {cursor_before = false}}))`\r\n4. Type a character\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n_No response_\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nIf you try it a couple of times, it will stop finding the right character, or the message \"(mini.jump2d) No spots to show\" will appear. Note that both `word_start` and `line_start` work as expected.\r\n\r\nI'm using the `main` branch, BTW",
    "closed_at": "2023-06-05T08:21:12Z",
