            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\r\n\r\nYes, at the moment `builtin_opts.single_character` depends on being the same table. It is because internally it operates by [using `hooks.before_start`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/b1a6d9692e2f67ee35f77792b61eb7d44651c535/lua/mini/jump2d.lua#L543-L553) to define its `spotter` and definition is done in that **exact** table.\r\n\r\nThere are two solutions to this problem:\r\n- If you intend to use `single_character` only with one set of settings, you can override it like so:\r\n    ```lua\r\n    _G.jump2d_single_char = require('mini.jump2d').builtin_opts.single_character\r\n    _G.jump2d_single_char.allowed_lines.cursor_before = false\r\n    ```\r\n    And then use it as `:lua MiniJump2d.start(_G.jump2d_single_char)`.\r\n- Implement it explicitly (albeit losing some notification functionality):\r\n\r\n   ```lua\r\n    _G.my_jump2d_single_char = {\r\n      spotter = function() return {} end,\r\n      allowed_lines = { blank = false, fold = false, cursor_before = false },\r\n    }\r\n    _G.my_jump2d_single_char.hooks = {\r\n      before_start = function()\r\n        local pattern = vim.pesc(vim.fn.getcharstr())\r\n        _G.my_jump2d_single_char.spotter = MiniJump2d.gen_pattern_spotter(pattern)\r\n      end,\r\n    }\r\n   ```\r\n\r\n   And then use it as `:lua MiniJump2d.start(_G.my_jump2d_single_char)`.\r\n\r\nTo fully allow that, every element of `builtin_opts` should be configurable, but I don't I will happen as it will be a breaking change.\r\n\r\nI might consider moving everything to a callable `gen_opts` to be more aligned with other modules, though.",
